ng with this storm. If caught on the\nopen water stay below deck if possible, keep away from ungrounded\nmetal objects.\n\nReport severe weather to the Coast Guard or the National Weather\nService. You can also share your report with NWS Miami on Facebook\nand Twitter.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["SMWMFL"],"WMOidentifier":["WHUS52 KMFL 291806"],"eventMotionDescription":["2026-08-29T18:06:00-00:00...storm...120DEG...15KT...27.02,-80.65"],"waterspoutDetection":["POSSIBLE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.KMFL.MA.W.0246.260829T1806Z-260829T1830Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-29T14:30:00-04:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["SMW"],"NationalWeatherService":["MAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1f12e54866dbe297df5336b1953067bd10aeed14.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-87.5,38.87],[-87.46,38.74],[-87.64,38.46],[-87.78,38.47],[-87.56,38.73],[-87.56,38.86],[-87.5,38.87]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1f12e54866dbe297df5336b1953067bd10aeed14.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1f12e54866dbe297df5336b1953067bd10aeed14.001.1","areaDesc":"Lawrence, IL; Wabash, IL; Knox, IN","geocode":{"SAME":["017101","017185","018083"],"UGC":["ILC101","ILC185","INC083"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/ILC101","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/ILC185","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/INC083"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.55513f7e9c408f5bc1ea8c3d4b8ca021151f81f3.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.55513f7e9c408f5bc1ea8c3d4b8ca021151f81f3.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-08-28T20:36:00-05:00"}],"sent":"2026-08-29T10:11:00-05:00","effective":"2026-08-29T10:11:00-05:00","onset":"2026-08-29T10:11:00-05:00","expires":"2026-08-29T22:15:00-05:00","ends":"2026-08-30T09:10:00-05:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Indianapolis IN","headline":"Flood Warning issued August 29 at 10:11AM CDT until August 30 at 9:10AM CDT by NWS Indianapolis IN","description":"...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in\nIllinois...Indiana...\n\nWabash River at Vincennes\n\n...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in\nIllinois...Indiana...\n\nWabash River at Hutsonville Legacy Power Plant Site\n\nWabash River at Riverton\n\n.Minor flooding continues on the Wabash River from Hutsonville down\nto Vincennes. The river has crested. Flooding should come to an end\non the Wabash over the weekend.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Wabash River at Vincennes.\n\n* WHEN...Until Sunday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 17.0 feet, Considerable agricultural flooding extends\nfrom just north of the junction of Illinois 33 with Business 50 to\nthe St. Francesville, Illinois area.  River Road from Lincoln\nMemorial Bridge to Billett Rd is impassable.  Extensive seep water\nforms behind Illinois levees extending from Russellville to U.S.\nHighway 50.  Flooding of agricultural land begins in Knox County\nIndiana west of the railroad extending for the Oaktown area to the\nnorth side of Vincennes.  Extensive flooding of Small Creek.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 9:45 AM CDT /10:45 AM EDT/ Saturday the stage was 17.1 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 10.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 9:45 AM CDT /10:45 AM EDT/ Saturday was 18.1 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage late\nthis evening and continue falling to 4.4 feet Tuesday, September\n08.\n- Flood stage is 16.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/ind.\n\nThe next statement will be issued this evening at 1015 PM CDT /1115\nPM EDT/.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSIND"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS83 KIND 291511"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL SUNDAY MORNING"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KIND.FL.W.0174.000000T0000Z-260830T1410Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-30T09:10:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7d6d2ad6897bfc2053b7ba54c44a8a9b438cb92a.001.1,2026-08-28T09:43:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cd9499db912cf41eedf6e7ed89ab331259907008.002.1,2026-08-27T20:38:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6315cb2dc8d0f54eaa778ad01fb00cd0c181d340.002.1,2026-08-27T10:04:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.370c270d7d1b162addcf02dc7258854c454ad061.002.1,2026-08-26T13:04:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.12919d77a71ad3fa4d2d46fe4c889e8395a827c1.003.1,2026-08-26T09:14:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.21fed40f8a4270468743863bc5d2282950a3b72d.003.1,2026-08-25T13:12:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.966efdc66b3086f5aa2b21cb1cfbfa88e06cea31.004.1,2026-08-25T08:35:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.485716edaea873f78d95b8660a4bf26eec3149e1.003.1,2026-08-24T12:54:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d17042b1f0925f697c4f2f6f4a97ea6a0fc7af62.003.1,2026-08-24T20:54:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e611d888f0b860bf842f3076e8bd792348b6b8d0.003.1,2026-08-24T08:54:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.946a70c1dd6536458e250ec5f6d5adee0ba9c93c.006.1,2026-08-23T21:48