ding is in progress.\nHigh water surrounds many river cabins.  Access to most river\ncabins is by boat only.  Levees begin to protect farmland.\nExtensive flooding of Leaverton Park occurs in Palestine, Illinois.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 10:00 AM CDT /11:00 AM EDT/ Saturday the stage was 18.1 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 10.5 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 10:00 AM CDT /11:00 AM EDT/ Saturday was 19.4 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage early\nMonday morning and continue falling to 5.1 feet Tuesday,\nSeptember 08.\n- Flood stage is 15.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/ind.\n\nThe next statement will be issued this evening at 1015 PM CDT /1115\nPM EDT/.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSIND"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS83 KIND 291511"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL MONDAY AFTERNOON"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KIND.FL.W.0162.000000T0000Z-260831T1800Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-31T13:00:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7d6d2ad6897bfc2053b7ba54c44a8a9b438cb92a.002.1,2026-08-28T09:43:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cd9499db912cf41eedf6e7ed89ab331259907008.004.1,2026-08-27T20:38:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6315cb2dc8d0f54eaa778ad01fb00cd0c181d340.003.1,2026-08-27T10:04:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.370c270d7d1b162addcf02dc7258854c454ad061.003.1,2026-08-26T13:04:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.12919d77a71ad3fa4d2d46fe4c889e8395a827c1.005.1,2026-08-26T09:14:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.